WEBVTT

00:04.240 --> 00:06.940
Huh? Ms. Eléonore did?

00:06.940 --> 00:10.950
Yes. She says she has a high
fever and can't tutor you...

00:10.950 --> 00:12.910
and that she'd like to quit entirely.

00:12.910 --> 00:14.740
Do you have any idea why?

00:14.740 --> 00:15.710
Uh...

00:20.090 --> 00:21.780
You have no shadow!

00:26.790 --> 00:30.120
N-No. Maybe the fever has her feeling down?

00:30.120 --> 00:31.440
Good grief.

00:31.440 --> 00:34.260
Guiding apprentices is part
of a pharmacian's training.

00:34.260 --> 00:35.510
What's gotten into her?

00:35.730 --> 00:36.410
Farma.

00:36.410 --> 00:37.090
Yes, sir?

00:37.320 --> 00:40.290
Deliver this potion and this letter to her.

00:40.550 --> 00:42.380
Y-Yes, Father.

00:49.510 --> 00:51.530
<i>Judging by the recipe Bruno told me,</i>

00:51.530 --> 00:54.960
<i>this potion will have no more
effect than a nutrient drink.</i>

00:55.530 --> 00:57.740
<i>If she really has a fever...</i>

00:57.740 --> 00:59.910
<i>Acetaminophen. As needed.</i>

00:59.910 --> 01:01.410
<i>Take for fever or pain.</i>

01:01.410 --> 01:04.600
<i>Wait four to six hours between doses.</i>

01:27.440 --> 01:33.910
<b>Parallel World Pharmacy</b>

02:35.000 --> 02:39.010
<b>Episode 2</b>

02:50.740 --> 02:54.440
For what purpose do you deign
to visit my humble home?

02:54.440 --> 02:56.140
E-E-Elen?!

02:56.140 --> 02:59.110
Have you come to eliminate me
for knowing your secret?

02:59.110 --> 03:00.440
That is why, is it not?!

03:00.440 --> 03:02.860
It's nothing like that,
so please calm down!

03:02.860 --> 03:05.340
Look! I didn't bring a wand or anything!

03:11.740 --> 03:12.900
In that case...

03:15.610 --> 03:17.160
why <i>are</i> you here?

03:17.160 --> 03:19.980
My father sent me.

03:19.980 --> 03:23.780
Since you said you have a fever,
he asked me to bring you this potion.

03:23.780 --> 03:26.170
Master made that for me?

03:26.170 --> 03:29.900
He went to that trouble when I
can make fever medicine myself?

03:31.100 --> 03:32.310
O-Oh, gods!

03:32.310 --> 03:33.700
Is it poisoned?!

03:33.700 --> 03:35.020
No! Don't be silly!

03:38.440 --> 03:40.870
Also, these are from me.

03:40.870 --> 03:43.560
A different type of fever
medicine to Father's,

03:43.560 --> 03:45.240
and a salve for your jammed finger,

03:45.240 --> 03:47.150
as well as some usage instructions.

03:48.920 --> 03:50.400
O-Oh, gods!

03:50.400 --> 03:52.000
Are they poisoned?!

03:52.000 --> 03:53.620
For the second time, no!

03:53.930 --> 03:56.780
I have no intention of harming you, Elen.

03:56.780 --> 04:00.510
The truth is, I also want you
to keep being my tutor.

04:00.510 --> 04:01.990
But why?

04:01.990 --> 04:05.920
You have no need for instruction
in Divine Arts or pharmacology.

04:05.920 --> 04:09.580
You are an incarnation of
the Panactheos, after all!

04:09.580 --> 04:12.570
As far as I know,
I'm human, not a god...

04:13.050 --> 04:16.840
If that is your wish,
then it is my command.

04:17.560 --> 04:21.570
I swear, nothing and no one
can pry your secret from my lips,

04:21.570 --> 04:23.990
including your father and your family!

04:23.990 --> 04:25.280
And so, I beg of you,

04:25.700 --> 04:28.220
please spare my wretched life!

04:29.720 --> 04:33.480
I really don't have a clue how to
use Divine Arts. That's the truth.

04:33.940 --> 04:35.350
Listen, Elen,

04:38.410 --> 04:41.370
I need you in my life.

04:43.280 --> 04:44.270
Huh?

04:44.270 --> 04:45.590
What do you...

04:45.590 --> 04:49.130
Ah, I mean, like, I need your knowledge.

04:49.130 --> 04:50.770
Oh, that's how you meant it.

04:51.130 --> 04:53.770
It looks like knowledge of Divine
Arts is passed down orally.

04:53.770 --> 04:56.800
The de Médicis library
has no materials on it.

04:56.800 --> 04:59.260
I have no way to learn it on my own.

04:59.260 --> 05:02.520
I don't know how to control my abilities.

05:02.740 --> 05:05.880
And so I want you to treat me
as you always have.

05:05.880 --> 05:07.560
Don't treat me like a superior.

05:08.450 --> 05:12.350
But if... if your mind is made up,
and I can't change it...

05:18.480 --> 05:22.820
then please take these as thanks
for all you did as my tutor.

05:23.330 --> 05:25.590
Thanks for everything, Elen.

05:26.190 --> 05:27.080
What?

05:34.220 --> 05:36.090
I won't disturb you any longer.

05:36.700 --> 05:39.800
Sorry for scaring you.
I hope you can get some rest.

05:44.000 --> 05:45.210
Take care of yourself.

05:58.370 --> 06:00.640
Do I take this?

06:01.420 --> 06:06.080
I've never even seen a medicine
in powdered form like this.

06:13.370 --> 06:14.270
What am I thinking?

06:14.780 --> 06:18.700
The Panactheos is a benevolent
Guardian Deity at heart.

06:18.700 --> 06:21.620
There are no stories of
the god harming humans.

06:26.450 --> 06:29.600
Cerulean flowers. My favorite...

06:32.360 --> 06:33.480
Here goes nothing!

06:39.730 --> 06:42.330
Good morning, Panactheos!

06:43.200 --> 06:44.360
Elen!

06:44.830 --> 06:46.700
Do you feel better now?

06:46.700 --> 06:49.650
I see you're still heavily fortified, though.

06:49.650 --> 06:51.820
It's a precaution, just in case.

06:51.820 --> 06:54.850
If I'm going to help the Panactheos train,

06:54.850 --> 06:57.810
it's only prudent to have some protection!

06:57.810 --> 06:59.260
So then you'll...

06:59.260 --> 07:04.740
Of course, Panactheos—excuse me,
Farma. I'll keep tutoring you.

07:04.740 --> 07:07.060
Thank you, Elen!

07:07.060 --> 07:09.590
No need to thank me.

07:09.590 --> 07:13.670
If you were to lose control of your
Divine Arts due to my lack of instruction,

07:13.670 --> 07:15.550
you could level the entire imperial city!

07:15.550 --> 07:17.300
No need to exaggerate.

07:17.300 --> 07:19.540
Do you really think I'm exaggerating?

07:21.930 --> 07:25.700
Besides, I'm the one who
should be thanking you.

07:25.980 --> 07:30.890
That salve and that bitter powder
seem to have worked marvelously!

07:30.890 --> 07:32.430
I'm glad to hear that.

07:32.430 --> 07:37.250
Not even Master's medicine works so quickly.

07:37.250 --> 07:38.500
Thank you.

07:38.500 --> 07:39.800
Don't mention it.

07:39.800 --> 07:42.650
And I loved the flowers.

07:46.140 --> 07:49.290
Now then, next stop:
an uninhabited island!

07:49.290 --> 07:50.600
Uninhabited island?

07:50.600 --> 07:52.910
As I said, we're taking precautions!

08:30.360 --> 08:34.340
Good grief! Now I'm totally covered in sand!

08:34.340 --> 08:35.870
Ugh, sorry...

08:36.290 --> 08:39.610
You'll eventually gain control of your Arts.

08:39.610 --> 08:41.740
I guess we'll just have to keep practicing!

08:59.810 --> 09:01.970
Why, hello, Young Master!

09:02.280 --> 09:04.220
I hope you're well, Madeleine.

09:11.990 --> 09:13.820
Reflux esophagitis.

09:16.880 --> 09:18.740
Fine weather today, eh, sir?

09:18.970 --> 09:21.160
You've certainly got pep
in your step, Alfred.

09:22.960 --> 09:24.150
Stye.

09:31.360 --> 09:33.910
The master will be delayed
in returning tonight.

09:34.490 --> 09:36.430
Please inform the head chef.

09:35.350 --> 09:36.590
Pharyngitis.

09:37.380 --> 09:38.800
Yes, at once.

09:38.800 --> 09:40.770
Chronic simple rhinitis.

09:43.060 --> 09:46.280
Simon, sir. I have a financial
matter to discuss.

09:44.670 --> 09:47.020
Gonarthrosis.

09:47.930 --> 09:51.900
A non-invasive treatment might
be best for Cédric's knees.

09:54.120 --> 09:56.830
When full recovery is possible,
the light disappears.

09:56.830 --> 10:00.130
When it's not possible,
a dim glow remains...

10:02.330 --> 10:04.790
No fever or rash. No findings on fingers.
Swelling in both knees. Tenderness on inside.
Joint movement is deteriorating, but still smooth.
Gonarthrosis, both knees. (Confirmed via Diagnostic Eye)
Pain observed. Having effect on daily life.
Should avoid heavy lifting as much as possible.
Confirmed presence of kidney damage. Prescribe NSAIDs.

10:04.790 --> 10:06.000
...should be considered.

10:09.270 --> 10:11.970
<i>In this world, my existence is "heresy."</i>

10:12.540 --> 10:16.320
<i>If my lack of shadow and my special
abilities are discovered,</i>

10:16.320 --> 10:19.300
<i>in the worst case, I might
be arrested and executed.</i>

10:24.730 --> 10:30.470
<i>To prevent that, I need to make myself
indispensable—at least to the people here.</i>

10:31.010 --> 10:32.650
Rhagadiform eczema.

10:41.380 --> 10:43.520
That's a pharmacian's mansion for you!

10:43.520 --> 10:46.080
All the classic tools for
compounding medicine are here!

10:46.270 --> 10:51.340
<i>First, I'll make a moisturizing
heparinoid cream for Lotte.</i>

10:51.340 --> 10:53.760
<i>I'll synthesize the base
ingredients in turn.</i>

10:57.280 --> 10:58.490
<i>Glycerol!</i>

11:08.260 --> 11:09.880
<i>Great! It worked!</i>

11:09.880 --> 11:12.070
<i>As long as I know the
substance's composition,</i>

11:12.070 --> 11:15.820
<i>I can create both solids and liquids,
and even viscous substances.</i>

11:18.330 --> 11:22.600
<i>For the emulsifier and surfactant,
I'll use glycerol monostearate.</i>

11:23.240 --> 11:28.010
<i>After producing heparin, I'll depolymerize
it to obtain the main heparinoid medicine.</i>

11:28.010 --> 11:30.610
<i>The oil phase will be an oleaginous
base with squalene and cetyl alcohol.</i>

11:30.080 --> 11:33.730
<i>Then I take the oil phase and
the water phase with the base</i>

11:33.730 --> 11:35.570
<i>and ingredients mixed in and
warm them both with water,</i>

11:35.570 --> 11:39.310
<i>gradually add the water
phase to the oil phase</i>

11:39.310 --> 11:41.630
<i>with the emulsifier added, and stir quickly.</i>

11:40.860 --> 11:42.400
<i>To finish, essential oils for fragrance</i>

11:42.400 --> 11:45.920
<i>and then safe preservatives
and stabilizers for shelf life.</i>

11:45.920 --> 11:48.050
<i>Now I just combine until it's homogenous...</i>

11:49.010 --> 11:50.220
<i>Finished!</i>

11:56.630 --> 11:59.700
Huh? A... gift for me?

11:59.700 --> 12:02.910
Yup, because you're always
doing so much for me.

12:05.300 --> 12:08.310
You said all the scrubbing you do
dries out your hands, right?

12:08.310 --> 12:10.660
Put this cream on the dry spots.

12:10.660 --> 12:14.880
Put this steroid salve on
the particularly bad spots.

12:16.620 --> 12:20.600
Master Farma! Thank you
so much! I'm so happy!

12:22.300 --> 12:24.830
Can I share this with my mom?

12:24.830 --> 12:26.690
She has the same problem...

12:26.690 --> 12:28.830
Oh! And the other servants as well!

12:28.830 --> 12:32.320
I'll make some for each of them after
examining their symptoms individually.

12:32.320 --> 12:33.520
By the way,

12:33.520 --> 12:35.730
I have gifts for everyone else as well.

12:52.570 --> 12:57.270
Everyone was overjoyed to receive
your medicines, Master Farma!

12:57.270 --> 13:01.040
Yeah. I never imagined Madeleine
would cry that much.

13:01.390 --> 13:03.010
Or that you would, either.

13:03.010 --> 13:04.960
Well, I mean...

13:04.960 --> 13:05.970
Yes?

13:05.970 --> 13:10.680
We servants have <i>never</i> received
medicine from our masters before.

13:10.680 --> 13:12.160
Of course we were touched.

13:12.160 --> 13:13.180
You haven't?

13:13.180 --> 13:15.980
Even though the servants
are practically family?

13:15.980 --> 13:17.750
That's just how it is.

13:18.290 --> 13:21.900
The master is a pharmacian
for high-class individuals.

13:21.900 --> 13:25.080
Aristocratic pharmacians
don't examine commoners.

13:25.080 --> 13:26.940
That is simply our station.

13:27.230 --> 13:31.160
It doesn't seem right to select
patients based on social class.

13:32.390 --> 13:34.680
Even if they did examine us,

13:34.680 --> 13:38.110
the cost of the medicine is
out of reach for commoners.

13:45.100 --> 13:48.070
<i>A class-based society and
drug price problems...</i>

13:48.070 --> 13:50.010
<i>With the state of knowledge in this era,</i>

13:50.010 --> 13:52.590
<i>I bet few medicines even work.</i>

13:52.590 --> 13:55.160
<i>On top of that, without
the money for medicine,</i>

13:55.160 --> 13:57.590
<i>the commoners have to turn
to superstitions and shams.</i>

13:57.590 --> 13:58.840
<i>And mortality rates are high...</i>

13:59.320 --> 14:02.280
<i>If more effective medicines
were made more common...</i>

14:02.280 --> 14:06.920
You had never examined me before,
either, Master Farma.

14:06.920 --> 14:08.800
What? R-Really?

14:08.800 --> 14:13.190
Really. Though, I'm sure that was partly
because the master prohibited it.

14:13.190 --> 14:14.230
Ah.

14:14.540 --> 14:16.760
It's true that it would be
dangerous for an apprentice

14:16.760 --> 14:20.000
to treat people with half-baked knowledge.

14:22.130 --> 14:26.570
But going forward, I want to make medicine
available to those who need it.

14:26.570 --> 14:29.370
And that should also serve as
part of my pharmacian's training.

14:29.370 --> 14:31.370
You're such a kind person!

14:31.370 --> 14:33.180
I don't think I'm especially kind...

14:35.130 --> 14:41.070
With all you've done lately to treat
people regardless of social class,

14:41.070 --> 14:43.110
I'm sure you'll make a great pharmacian!

14:44.060 --> 14:46.820
I'll work as hard as I can
to make that come true.

14:58.620 --> 14:59.970
Good morning!

15:02.320 --> 15:04.040
Oh? Where's Blanche?

15:06.520 --> 15:07.770
Mother?

15:07.770 --> 15:08.700
Farma.

15:09.210 --> 15:11.550
Blanche came down with chickenpox.

15:15.310 --> 15:18.730
<i>Chickenpox, also known as varicella,</i>

15:18.730 --> 15:24.450
<i>is a contagious infectious disease caused by
infection with the varicella-zoster virus,</i>

15:24.450 --> 15:26.480
<i>classified as human herpesvirus 3.</i>

15:26.480 --> 15:29.010
<i>They have chickenpox in this world, too?</i>

15:29.470 --> 15:31.140
<i>If it's the same as on Earth,</i>

15:31.140 --> 15:34.700
<i>then a four-year-old should most
likely experience only mild illness.</i>

15:34.970 --> 15:37.910
<i>Is the disease really so dangerous here?</i>

15:37.910 --> 15:41.890
Stay away from Blanche for three weeks,
or the disease may spread.

15:41.890 --> 15:45.120
We have to leave the poor girl
alone for three entire weeks?

15:45.120 --> 15:49.630
We'll have a small number of servants
care for her, just as we did with Farma.

15:49.630 --> 15:51.210
Do you remember that, four years ago?

15:52.390 --> 15:57.400
<i>He's hinting that I can go see her
because of my immunity...</i>

15:57.400 --> 15:58.690
But exercise caution.

15:58.950 --> 16:02.170
Even after you've had chickenpox,
the disease can reoccur,

16:02.170 --> 16:04.650
though that fact is not yet
recorded in medical texts.

16:05.360 --> 16:06.320
Simon.

16:06.320 --> 16:07.120
Yes, Master.

16:07.120 --> 16:10.790
<i>Even on Earth, it was thought until only
recently that immunity was lifelong.</i>

16:10.790 --> 16:13.860
<i>He knows that reinfection
occurs in rare cases?</i>

16:14.540 --> 16:16.380
<i>This man is incredible.</i>

16:16.380 --> 16:18.920
I've been summoned for
an emergency house call.

16:18.920 --> 16:21.120
Be sure to exercise due caution.

16:24.260 --> 16:25.260
Yes, Father.

16:33.490 --> 16:37.190
<i>When it comes to chickenpox medications
that are appropriate for children,</i>

16:39.680 --> 16:42.140
<i>my options are acyclovir and valacyclovir.</i>

16:43.850 --> 16:48.410
<i>Since I'm making it myself, acyclovir, with
its less complex molecule, seems better.</i>

16:48.740 --> 16:49.560
<i>In short...</i>

16:59.740 --> 17:07.460
2-amino-9-[(2-hydroxyethoxy)methyl]-
1,9-dihydro-6H-purin-6-one.

17:10.770 --> 17:12.560
Create acyclovir!

17:25.570 --> 17:27.530
Blanche, are you awake?

17:27.860 --> 17:29.630
Brother?

17:34.480 --> 17:35.710
How do you feel?

17:36.240 --> 17:38.330
I feel yucky.

17:38.330 --> 17:41.280
I have all these bumpies, and I'm itchy.

17:41.280 --> 17:43.570
<i>She has the characteristic red rash.</i>

17:43.920 --> 17:47.710
<i>Chickenpox. Human herpesvirus 3 infection.</i>

17:48.220 --> 17:53.990
Brother, Father will be upset
that you came to my room.

17:54.420 --> 17:58.230
That's why I snuck in to
see you. It's a secret.

17:58.710 --> 18:00.280
A secret...

18:02.860 --> 18:04.900
Blanche, I have medicine for you.

18:05.940 --> 18:08.350
I don't wanna! It's bitter and yucky!

18:09.810 --> 18:12.800
Let's put the bitter medicine in a macaron!

18:17.400 --> 18:19.480
Is it okay to do that?

18:19.480 --> 18:21.560
It is with this medicine.

18:21.560 --> 18:24.690
For some medicines it's bad,
so always ask me first.

18:24.690 --> 18:25.630
Okay!

18:25.630 --> 18:27.960
Make sure you drink lots of
water after you eat this.

18:34.120 --> 18:35.920
Hey, Brother?

18:35.920 --> 18:37.020
What is it?

18:37.020 --> 18:40.760
Father said there was no
medicine for what I have.

18:40.760 --> 18:44.550
Uh... I found it in a new book!

18:44.900 --> 18:46.830
One of Father's books?

18:46.830 --> 18:49.610
But Father doesn't know about it?

18:49.610 --> 18:53.850
F-Father is very busy, so maybe he
hasn't had time to read it yet!

18:53.850 --> 18:57.010
So this will be our little
secret, too. Okay?

18:57.010 --> 18:58.070
Okey-dokey!

18:58.510 --> 18:59.720
It's itchy!

19:00.270 --> 19:01.880
Ah, don't scratch!

19:01.880 --> 19:04.240
If the blisters break open,
the virus will get out.

19:04.240 --> 19:05.960
Vi-rus?

19:05.960 --> 19:10.150
<i>In this world, there's no concept
of viruses or bacteria...</i>

19:10.410 --> 19:12.490
Brother, teach me! Teach me!

19:12.490 --> 19:14.510
What's a vi-rus?

19:14.510 --> 19:19.370
It's... sorta like an evil spirit
that's too small to see.

19:20.310 --> 19:21.490
A ghost?

19:22.080 --> 19:23.110
I'm scared!

19:23.430 --> 19:24.860
Don't worry.

19:24.860 --> 19:28.320
After we apply this azulene ointment,
I'll stay with you for a while.

19:30.650 --> 19:32.970
Brother, you're different.

19:32.970 --> 19:33.620
What?

19:33.620 --> 19:35.660
Is something different than before?

19:35.660 --> 19:38.350
Wh-What makes you say that?

19:38.350 --> 19:43.210
I mean, you never used to
play with me like this.

19:44.850 --> 19:48.560
And you never fed me like this either.

19:48.560 --> 19:51.050
Brother, you got really, really nice!

19:51.800 --> 19:54.020
Is the way I am now weird?

19:54.020 --> 19:56.740
Umm, I dunno.

19:57.010 --> 19:57.970
But,

19:57.970 --> 20:01.300
I wuv this Brother, too!

20:02.520 --> 20:05.520
Bro-bro, I wuv you!

20:09.670 --> 20:14.080
Brother, is something in
your eyesies? Are you okay?

20:19.980 --> 20:22.680
How is your appetite? Any pain?

20:22.680 --> 20:26.020
No ouchies! I'm hungy!

20:26.020 --> 20:29.150
Hmm. Your recovery seems awfully quick.

20:29.150 --> 20:32.180
Well, you see, Father...

20:35.380 --> 20:36.480
It's a secret!

20:45.490 --> 20:50.430
I gotta say, it seems like I'm abnormal, even
by the standards of a parallel world situation.

20:51.090 --> 20:54.690
I have Substance Creation and Elimination,

20:54.690 --> 20:57.350
my left hand lets me see medical problems,

20:57.690 --> 21:01.020
and my right even lets me magnify things...

21:01.730 --> 21:05.950
And I have no shadow.
Is it because I've died once already?

21:06.660 --> 21:09.170
These powers are too great.

21:09.170 --> 21:12.150
Can I really keep using them
at no cost to myself?

21:14.510 --> 21:16.880
What's going to happen to me?

21:22.350 --> 21:23.540
I did it!

21:24.300 --> 21:26.890
One Leeuwenhoek simple microscope!

21:27.510 --> 21:33.170
Now I can observe things at high
resolution without using my right hand!

21:33.170 --> 21:37.520
Even if viruses are too small,
I bet I could show Blanche bacteria.

21:39.270 --> 21:42.560
Master Farma, pardon the interruption.

21:42.560 --> 21:43.840
Come in.

21:44.940 --> 21:46.720
The master wishes to see you.

21:46.720 --> 21:48.030
Please come at once.

21:55.580 --> 21:57.220
Ah, you're here, Farma.

21:57.780 --> 21:59.880
Get ready to leave immediately.

22:01.370 --> 22:03.760
We have an emergency house call
